**WatermelonDB** is the industry standard for this task because it is built for high-performance offline-first apps; it loads data lazily and uses a persistent SQLite bridge to ensure your app stays fast even with thousands of survey records.

### 1. Define the Schema
First, define your survey data structure.
```typescript
// model/schema.ts
import { appSchema, tableSchema } from '@nozbe/watermelondb'

export default appSchema({
  version: 1,
  tables: [
    tableSchema({
      name: 'surveys',
      columns: [
        { name: 'survey_data', type: 'string' },
        { name: 'status', type: 'string' }, // 'pending' or 'synced'
        { name: 'created_at', type: 'number' },
      ],
    }),
  ],
})
```

### 2. The Sync Logic
This function handles the "Offline-First" nature. It checks if the device is online; if so, it pushes the local changes to your server and pulls updates.

```typescript
// sync/sync.ts
import { synchronize } from '@nozbe/watermelondb/sync'
import NetInfo from "@react-native-community/netinfo";

export async function syncDatabase(database: any) {
  const state = await NetInfo.fetch();

  if (!state.isConnected) return; // Keep working offline

  await synchronize({
    database,
    pullChanges: async ({ lastPulledAt }) => {
      const response = await fetch(`https://api.yourservice.com/sync?last_pulled=${lastPulledAt}`);
      return await response.json();
    },
    pushChanges: async ({ changes, lastPulledAt }) => {
      await fetch(`https://api.yourservice.com/sync`, {
        method: 'POST',
        body: JSON.stringify({ changes }),
      });
    },
  });
}
```

### 3. Implementing the Survey Entry Screen
This component saves data locally to the database. Because of the offline-first architecture, the user doesn't need an internet connection to perform this action.

```tsx
// components/SurveyForm.tsx
import { database } from '../model/database';

const saveSurvey = async (data: string) => {
  await database.write(async () => {
    await database.get('surveys').create((survey: any) => {
      survey.surveyData = data;
      survey.status = 'pending';
      survey.createdAt = Date.now();
    });
  });

  // Trigger sync in background
  syncDatabase(database);
};
```

### 4. Background Sync Listener
To ensure data syncs automatically when the user regains a signal, listen to the device's connectivity status.

```tsx
// App.tsx
import NetInfo from "@react-native-community/netinfo";

useEffect(() => {
  const unsubscribe = NetInfo.addEventListener(state => {
    if (state.isConnected) {
      console.log("Connection restored. Syncing...");
      syncDatabase(database);
