3.  **Poll-mode Drivers:** This code uses a tight polling loop. In production, you would pin this thread to a dedicated physical CPU core (`pthread_setaffinity_np`) to prevent the OS scheduler from moving your process and flushing the CPU cache.
4.  **Batching:** By processing packets in batches (e.g., 64 packets at a time), we amortize the cost of the system calls and memory barrier synchronization.

