```java
@Entity
public class Account {
    @Id
    private Long id;
    private BigDecimal balance;

    // Standard getters, setters, and a method to ensure thread-safe balance updates
    public void debit(BigDecimal amount) {
        if (this.balance.compareTo(amount) < 0) throw new InsufficientFundsException();
        this.balance = this.balance.subtract(amount);
    }

    public void credit(BigDecimal amount) {
        this.balance = this.balance.add(amount);
    }
}
```

#### 2. The Service Layer (Transactional Logic)
The `@Transactional` annotation is critical here; if the credit fails after the debit, the entire operation rolls back, preventing money from vanishing.

```java
@Service
public class PaymentService {

    @Autowired
    private AccountRepository accountRepository;

    @Transactional
    public void processPayment(Long fromAccountId, Long toAccountId, BigDecimal amount, String idempotencyKey) {
        // 1. Check for Idempotency: verify if request has already been processed
        if (transactionLog.exists(idempotencyKey)) {
            return; // Already processed, return success to avoid double-charging
        }

        // 2. Perform Atomic Transfer
        Account source = accountRepository.findById(fromAccountId).orElseThrow();
        Account target = accountRepository.findById(toAccountId).orElseThrow();

        source.debit(amount);
        target.credit(amount);

        // 3. Save state
        accountRepository.save(source);
        accountRepository.save(target);
        transactionLog.save(idempotencyKey, "SUCCESS");
    }
}
```

